WEBVTT

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:25.120
Hi, Grandpa.

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:28.120
Can I help?

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:29.460
Yes, indeed.

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:35.900
and I'll make you two fried eggs.

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:39.420
How about some bacon?

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:42.260
I made enough for an army.

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:45.020
You going to the baseball game today?

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:50.180
It's a perfect day for it--a little cloudy but nice and warm.

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:52.480
Dad and I were planning to go to the game,

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:53.980
but he has to work today,

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:55.660
and my friends don't want to go.

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:57.640
It's not an important game, anyway.

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:00.380
Do you have any other plans for the day

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:02.500
I'll work on my computer.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:05.960
I have a new math program, and I want to learn how to use it.

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:07.700
Maybe you can teach me

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.280
how to work on a computer someday.

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:13.160
Anytime. It's really easy, but, like anything,

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:14.860
you need to work at it, Grandpa.

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:18.920
This bacon is great.

00:01:19.420 --> 00:01:20.600
I love crispy bacon.

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:23.100
Oh, what are you doing tomorrow?

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:25.320
Nothing much.

00:01:26.010 --> 00:01:31.520
Well, maybe your dad and I could take you fishing with us.

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:33.920
I'd like that, but ...

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:37.740
But Dad is always so busy.

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:42.200
Well, can you come fishing with me tomorrow?

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:45.900
Sure, I can.

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:50.660
Robbie says you can't take him to the game today.

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:52.560
I really feel bad about it,

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:55.140
in the children's ward.

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:56.620
I understand.

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:00.420
Maybe we can spend some time together next weekend.

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:01.560
Definitely.

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:02.700
We should.

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:05.040
You and Robbie and me.

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:08.180
Remember our first fishing trip?

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:09.680
I sure do....

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:13.740
Well, I've got to run, Dad.

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:14.940
See you later.

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:20.620
I'm thinking about it....

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:26.060
Oh, the usual problems.

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:28.920
You're working pretty hard these days.

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:30.920
I guess I am.

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:36.900
When did you last go fishing with Robbie?

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:39.020
I remember exactly.

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:46.780
We didn't catch anything.

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:50.140
Remember our fishing trips?

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:53.260
Yes. I loved them.

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:58.300
Remember catching your first fish?

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:02.190
I fell out of the boat!

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:07.500
We had some good times together.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:09.280
Yes, we did.

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:12.320
Maybe we should do it again.

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:17.640
Don't you have to work?

00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:20.590
My paper work will wait.

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:24.900
I am, too, Son.

00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:28.260
Tomorrow.

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:31.420
It'll be like old times for you and me.

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:33.540
And Robbie will love it.

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:37.700
Well, what's the weather going to be like?

00:03:38.210 --> 00:03:41.130
Radio says sunny and mild.

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:47.820
Well, I'll tell Robbie.

00:03:53.660 --> 00:03:54.720
Don't thank me.

00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:56.940
I'm just being a grandfather.
